## 2. Issues Found in Software_Requirements_Specification.md

### Requirements vs Implementation Status

| Requirement | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| FR1: Login | Implemented | [AuthController](file:///c:/Users/Bhuvan%20Chandran%20S/Downloads/ClearWay%20app/smart-routes-api/src/main/java/com/cleanroute/api/controller/AuthController.java) handles signup/login |
| FR2: Checking routes | Implemented | One-off route checking works via TomTom alternatives |
| FR3: Daily Checks / Scheduling | Partially | [PollutionScheduler](file:///c:/Users/Bhuvan%20Chandran%20S/Downloads/ClearWay%20app/smart-routes-api/src/main/java/com/cleanroute/api/scheduler) runs every 15 min, but user-configured time preferences are not yet implemented |
| FR4: Warnings | Partially | NotificationEngineService has threshold logic, but no actual push delivery channel (FCM/email) is wired |
| FR5: Route Finding | Implemented | TomTom provides up to 3 alternatives, ranked by pollution |
| FR6: One-off trips | Implemented | Same as FR5 |
| FR7: Custom Allergies | Implemented | Four pollutant toggles in User entity + weighted scoring |
| NFR2: Map Accuracy | Done (differently) | Doc says "going to use OpenRouteService" but TomTom was used instead. Should update. |
| NFR3: Reliability | Not implemented | No fallback handling when TomTom or Open-Meteo API is unavailable |
| NFR5: Privacy | Partially | Passwords are hashed, but no HTTPS enforcement, no rate limiting, no token-based auth (sessions) |

### Missing Requirements

The SRS should add requirements for features that are already built but not documented:
- **FR8: Allergy Preference Management** -- Users can update their pollutant sensitivities after registration.
- **FR9: Alternative Route Comparison** -- System must present multiple routes ranked by pollution exposure.

