## 5. Suggested New Features (Priority Ordered)

These are features that would meaningfully improve the project beyond the current MVP.

### High Priority

| Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **JWT Token Authentication** | Replace the current stateless login (returns user object) with proper JWT tokens. Every API call should send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. This is the biggest security gap. | Medium |
| **API Error Fallback** | If TomTom or Open-Meteo API is unreachable, return cached/last-known data instead of a 500 error. Addresses NFR3. | Low |
| **Input Validation and Rate Limiting** | Add `@Valid` annotations on DTOs, proper error response DTOs, and Spring Security rate limiting. | Low |

### Medium Priority

| Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Route History Dashboard** | Frontend page showing a user's saved routes with historical pollution trends (line chart over time from `route_metrics`). The data is already being collected by PollutionScheduler. | Medium |
| **Password Reset Flow** | Email-based password reset. Currently there is no recovery mechanism. | Medium |
| **Full Dockerization** | Add the Spring Boot backend and React frontend as containers in `docker-compose.yml` alongside the DB. This would make the entire app one `docker compose up` command. | Medium |

### Low Priority (Nice-to-Have)

| Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Push Notification Delivery** | Wire up the existing FCM token field to actually send Firebase push notifications when pollution spikes. | Medium |
| **Dark Mode Toggle** | The UI currently has a fixed theme. A dark/light toggle would improve UX. | Low |
| **Export Routes to GPX/KML** | Allow users to download their route as a GPX file for use in fitness apps. | Low |

